# "probable" in moral and circular both mean argument regarding matter of fact and existence, the moral reasoning S1 divides from demonstrative reasoning. "Demonstrative" keeps the S1 sense of concerning relations of ideas throughout.
# A1 adds "sound" to the probable argument. I read that as narrowing which arguments count, not as a second sense of "probable". So A1 is not a bridge.
